    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d310">

                <pb facs="0444" n="359" sameAs="frus:frus1919v02/pg359"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">838.51/793: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Minister in
                        Haiti</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Bailly-Blanchard</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-02-27T18:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">February 27,
                                1919, 6 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>From McIlhenny.</p>
                <p>Immediately on sending cable of February 6, 1919, Bank began printing of gourdes
                    which as soon as printed will be at once forwarded to Haiti, but Bank will not
                    release gourdes until note or agreement has been signed. The plan of the retreat
                    has been carefully worked out here by the Department and Financial Adviser with
                    the Bank and is believed to be in desirable form for acceptance, <pb facs="0445"
                        n="360" xml:id="pg360"/> therefore I strongly advise the signing of note or
                    agreement without waiting for signing of retreat. Bank obligates itself to sign
                    retreat which meets approval of Department and Financial Adviser.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Polk</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
